From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: howeasy <howardabudd@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:36:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] slink: Polished Crystal variant forms in the pool

Owner ruling 2026-10-04: a regional/variant form is a different Pokemon
from its species, a cosmetic form is the same one. getPokemon() now holds
every BaseData record, the 46 variant forms (records 292..337) included,
so wild, trainer, starter, static and trade pools draw them with their
own stats and types; UPR alt-forme options stay off. EGG, the unused $100
and Unown stay banned.

A site reads as the record its (species, form) resolves to (variant form,
else the species), so formed wild slots, trainer mons, script sites and
trade sides join the model. writeSpecies is the one writer: a site that
still holds the same record is untouched (a cosmetic form stays);
otherwise LOW(species), then the site gender/egg bits, HIGH(species) << 5
and the variant form, the site own NO_FORM/PLAIN_FORM, or the context
plain spelling. The ini supplement adds the five resolved formed script
sites as StaticSite44..48.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 FORK_CHANGES.md                               |  15 ++
 PokeRandoZX-forms.jar                         | Bin 0 -> 1145956 bytes
 .../pkrandom/config/polished_offsets.ini      |  12 +-
 .../PolishedCrystalRomHandler.java            | 160 +++++++++---------
 4 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 80 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 PokeRandoZX-forms.jar

diff --git a/FORK_CHANGES.md b/FORK_CHANGES.md
index 63754fe..39102fa 100644
--- a/FORK_CHANGES.md
+++ b/FORK_CHANGES.md
@@ -163,3 +163,18 @@ entries), so a vanilla `[Red (U)]`-style entry executes exactly the original cod
   (`ld hl, wSlinkMailbox` and the 'S','L','N','K' beacon stores of `SlinkService`, patch/polished/src/slink.asm),
   instead of "any non-$FF byte in bank $7E". A release with the bridge signatures and one stray byte in bank $7E
   is no longer taken for an overlay; the ABI-version byte that follows is not pinned, so an ABI bump still matches.
+
+## Patch 21 — Polished Crystal variant forms in the pool
+- Owner ruling 2026-10-04: a regional/variant form (the 46 `VariantSpeciesAndFormTable` records 292..337) is a
+  different Pokemon from its species; a cosmetic form (Unown letters, Magikarp patterns, Arbok/Pikachu looks,
+  Dunsparce segments) is the same one. `getPokemon()` now returns every record, so wild, trainer, starter, static
+  and trade pools draw the variant forms with their own BaseData stats and types (similar strength, type themes and
+  legendary bans see the form's record); UPR's alt-forme options stay off. EGG, the unused $100 and Unown stay banned.
+- A site reads as the record its (species, form) resolves to (a variant form, else the species), so wild slots,
+  trainer mons, script sites and both NPC trade sides with a formed mon are now in the model.
+- `writeSpecies` is the one writer: a site that still holds the same record is not touched (a cosmetic form stays);
+  otherwise LOW(species), then the site's gender/egg bits | HIGH(species) << 5 | form, the form being the variant's,
+  or the site's own NO_FORM/PLAIN_FORM for a species, or the context's plain spelling (NO_FORM for wild, trainer and
+  trade sites, PLAIN_FORM for givepoke/loadwildmon) when the site held a variant or cosmetic form.
+- `config/polished_offsets.ini` supplement: StaticSite44..48, the five resolved formed script sites (the Galarian
+  birds at Cherrygrove Bay, Alolan Exeggutor on Shamouti Island, Hisuian Typhlosion in the Violet Outskirts house).
